# 11. Queueable mein `transient` ka kya role hai?

Agar koi variable:

```apex
transient
```

declare kiya gaya hai, to Queueable ke serialization/deserialization ke time uski value preserve nahi hoti.

Example:

```apex
transient String data;
```

Queueable execute hone par ye value:

```text
null
```

ho sakti hai.

Simple rule:

> **Queueable ke across persist karna hai to variable ko `transient` mat banao.**

---

# 12. Queueable + Database Callout

Queueable ka ek powerful use-case hai:

> **External API call karna.**

For example:

```text
Salesforce
    ↓
Queueable
    ↓
External REST API
    ↓
Response
    ↓
Salesforce processing
```

Iske liye Queueable class ko:

```apex
implements Queueable, Database.AllowsCallouts
```

karna hota hai.

Example:

```apex
public class ApiQueueable
    implements Queueable, Database.AllowsCallouts {

    public void execute(QueueableContext context) {

        HttpRequest request = new HttpRequest();

        // Callout logic

    }
}
```

`Database.AllowsCallouts` ek **marker interface** hai.

Iska purpose Salesforce ko indicate karna hai:

> "Is Queueable job ko HTTP/web-service callout karne ki permission chahiye."

---

# 13. Queueable Chaining kya hai?

Ye Queueable ka sabse powerful feature hai.

Suppose tumhara process hai:

```text
Job 1
  ↓
Job 2
  ↓
Job 3
  ↓
Job 4
```

Matlab Job 2 tab execute ho jab Job 1 complete ho.

Job 3 tab jab Job 2 complete ho.

Isko kehte hain:

> **Queueable Chaining**

---

# 14. Chaining kaise karte hain?

First Queueable:

```apex
public class FirstJob implements Queueable {

    public void execute(QueueableContext context) {

        // First job processing

        System.enqueueJob(
            new SecondJob()
        );
    }
}
```

Yahan important cheez hai:

```apex
System.enqueueJob(new SecondJob());
```

`execute()` ke andar call kiya gaya hai.

Flow:

```text
FirstJob
   ↓
execute()
   ↓
Processing
   ↓
enqueue SecondJob
   ↓
SecondJob
```

---

# 15. Chaining mein ek important restriction

Ek executing Queueable job se tum **sirf ek child Queueable** enqueue kar sakte ho.

Allowed:

```text
Parent
  ↓
Child
```

Allowed:

```text
Job1
  ↓
Job2
  ↓
Job3
  ↓
Job4
```

Not supported:

```text
        Job2
       ↙   ↘
    Job3    Job4
```

Yani ek parent se multiple child jobs directly create karna chaining ke context mein supported nahi hai.

---

# 16. Queueable chaining ko real-world example se samjho

Suppose e-commerce system mein:

### Job 1

Orders process karo.

### Job 2

Processed orders ka invoice generate karo.

### Job 3

Invoice ko external system mein send karo.

### Job 4

Customer ko notification bhejo.

Flow:

```text
Order Processing
       ↓
Invoice Generation
       ↓
External API
       ↓
Notification
```

Har stage independent Queueable ho sakti hai.

Isse large process ko manageable pieces mein divide kar sakte ho.

