# 17. Queueable Job Delay

Kabhi-kabhi tum chahte ho ki Queueable immediately execute na ho.

For example:

```apex
Integer delayInMinutes = 5;

ID jobID = System.enqueueJob(
    new MyQueueableClass(),
    delayInMinutes
);
```

Meaning:

> Salesforce job ko **minimum 5 minutes ke delay** ke saath schedule kare.

Allowed delay:

```text
0 to 10 minutes
```

Important:

**Minimum delay ka matlab exactly 5 minutes par execution guaranteed nahi hai.**

Matlab Salesforce 5 minutes se pehle execute nahi karega, but actual execution resource availability par depend karegi.

---

# 18. Delay ka practical use

Suppose external API rate-limited hai.

Tum rapidly ye kar rahe ho:

```text
Job 1 → API
Job 2 → API
Job 3 → API
Job 4 → API
Job 5 → API
...
```

API overload ho sakti hai.

Delay use karke:

```text
Job 1
 ↓
5 min
 ↓
Job 2
 ↓
5 min
 ↓
Job 3
```

jaisa controlled processing design kar sakte ho.

---

# 19. Chained jobs + delay

Ye especially useful hai polling scenarios mein.

Example:

```text
Salesforce → External API
              ↓
          "Processing"
              
wait

Salesforce → External API
              ↓
          "Processing"
              
wait

Salesforce → External API
              ↓
          "Completed"
```

Agar tum immediately repeatedly API ko call karoge, unnecessary async jobs consume ho sakte hain.

Isliye delay useful hai.

