# 37. Ek real-world example

Suppose Salesforce mein `Order__c` records hain.

Requirement:

> Order confirm hone ke baad external ERP system ko order bhejna hai.

Direct trigger mein API callout karna problematic ho sakta hai.

Instead:

```text
Order Trigger
     ↓
Queueable enqueue
     ↓
Queueable executes
     ↓
ERP API Callout
     ↓
ERP Response
     ↓
Order status update
```

Code structure:

```apex
public class OrderSyncQueueable
    implements Queueable, Database.AllowsCallouts {

    private Id orderId;

    public OrderSyncQueueable(Id orderId) {
        this.orderId = orderId;
    }

    public void execute(QueueableContext context) {

        Order__c orderRecord = [
            SELECT Id, Name
            FROM Order__c
            WHERE Id = :orderId
            LIMIT 1
        ];

        // Make API callout

        // Process response

        // Update Order
    }
}
```

Trigger se:

```apex
System.enqueueJob(
    new OrderSyncQueueable(orderId)
);
```

Yahan Queueable ka real benefit clearly dikhta hai.

